598:Spearman $\rho$ of profit vs seed index (1..50) and Geweke z (first 20\% vs last 50\%): \Ag{am_multisignal} $\rho = -0.301$ (p = 0.034, marginal), z = 2.04 (borderline); baseline $\rho = 0.189$ (p = 0.188), z = -1.05; \Ag{am_learned} $\rho = -0.176$ (p = 0.221), z = 0.39. The marginal trend reflects higher profits in early seeds, not systematic drift; paired t-tests (per-seed differencing) are robust to it.
700:\item \textbf{LLM zero-shot classifiers are profit-competitive but balanced-inferior.} Raw accuracy (74--83\%) is inflated by class imbalance (a no-skill funnel-trio sampler scores 80.3\%); all five macro-recalls (50.0--61.3\%) sit below the hand-tuned classifier's 65.9\%. The only profit contrasts surviving 610-way Bonferroni (threshold $p < 8.2\times10^{-5}$): glm-4.7 +\$0.07/scenario (\pv{8.9e-06}) and Mistral +\$0.09 (\pv{1.2e-08}); DeepSeek is significantly negative (-\$0.10, \pv{4.9e-06}); qwen3.6's +\$0.10 (p = 8.1e-03) does not survive. \textbf{Prompting is not a substitute for labels in this environment.}
758:\textbf{Honest framing of the oracle:} The oracle is an upper bound validating environment consistency. The scientifically meaningful agents are \Ag{am_multisignal} (98.9\%, within \$4 of oracle but the \$3.87 gap is significant, p = 1.3e-13), \Ag{am_multisignal_learned} (98.7\%), \Ag{am_inferred} (single-signal, 75.7\%, 4-of-6), and the noisy agents. The hand-set \Ag{am_multisignal} uses true generative centroids; 98.9\% is the nearest-centroid lower bound, not the Bayes rate (prior-weighted MAP achieves $\approx$99.2\%). The fair single-signal comparator is \Ag{am_learned} (87.5\%, +\$155.38), not the handicapped \Ag{am_inferred}: learned-vs-learned gain +\$50.01, handicapped +\$101.87.
792:\textbf{Multiplicity:} All p-values survive Bonferroni (630 total family; \S7.3); \S8.21 rows keep the historical 610-way annotation. \textbf{Normality:} profit distributions are unimodal and approximately symmetric at seed level; paired t-test robust at n = 50. \textbf{Equivalence testing:} ``Within \$4 of the oracle'' is descriptive --- the \$3.87 gap is significant (p = 1.3e-13). ``Essentially matches'' claims should carry the caveat that differences are statistically detectable at n = 50 even when economically negligible.

